    "text": "In a photoelectric effect measurement, the stopping potential for a given metal is found to be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math> volt when radiation of wavelength <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">λ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math> is used. If radiation of wavelength <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">λ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi></math>is used with the same metal then the stopping potential (in volt ) will be",
